display-objects"><title>Figures and Tables</title><fig position="float" id="F1"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p><bold>Comorbidities and risk factors in inpatients and outpatients on admission</bold>. Coronary artery disease includes one or more of the following: myocardial infarction, percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI), coronary artery bypass graft (CABG). PAD, peripheral arterial disease.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="1471-2458-6-256-1"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F2"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p><bold>Missed BP goals: Percentages of patients with systolic BP &#x02265; 140 mmHg and/or diastolic BP &#x02265; 90 mmHg at discharge</bold>. DBP, diastolic blood pressure; SBP, systolic blood pressure.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="1471-2458-6-256-2"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F3"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p><bold>Change of systolic blood pressure from admission (abscissa) to discharge (ordinate) in inpatients and outpatients</bold>. LOWESS regression. Inpatients are represented by the red regression line, the outpatient values by the blue regression line. Values are corrected for reliability (i.e., for regression-to-the-mean effects).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="1471-2458-6-256-3"/></fig><fig position="float" id="F4"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p><bold>Antihypertensive medication on admission and at discharge</bold>. Figure displays the percentages of antihypertensives by class in inpatients and outpatients at admission and discharge. Arrows indicate whether the drugs are more or less frequently used at discharge. &#x02192; denotes <italic>more </italic>frequently prescribed at discharge compared to admission. &#x02190; denotes <italic>less </italic>frequently prescribed at discharge compared to admission</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="1471-2458-6-256-4"/></fig><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Reasons for changing medications</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td align="left"><bold>Reason</bold></td><td align="left"><bold>Inpatients </bold>(N = 6358) <bold>%</bold></td><td align="left"><bold>Outpatients </bold>(N = 2246) <bold>%</bold></td><td align="left"><bold>p value</bold></td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">Lack of efficacy</td><td align="left">58.6</td><td align="left">67.7</td><td align="left">&#x0003c;0.0001</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Not tolerated*</td><td align="left">7.3</td><td align="left">21.1</td><td align="left">&#x0003c;0.0001</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Cough (with ACE inhibitors)</td><td align="left">35.3</td><td align="left">62.1</td><td align="left">&#x0003c;0.0001</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Angioedema</td><td align="left">25.8</td><td align="left">20.6</td><td align="left">n.s.</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Others</td><td align="left">35.7</td><td align="left">20.4</td><td align="left">&#x0003c;0.0001</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x02003;Not reported</td><td align="left">7.5</td><td align="left">8.2</td><td align="left">n.s.</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Contraindication</td><td align="left">1.7</td><td align="left">1.3</td><td align="left">n.s</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Drug-drug interaction</td><td align="left">1.0</td><td align="left">0.6</td><td align="left">n.s</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Compliance</td><td align="left">2.7</td><td align="left">4.2</td><td align="left">n.s</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Patient's request</td><td align="left">2.9</td><td align="left">5.3</td><td align="left">&#x0003c;0.0001</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Other reasons</td><td align="left">14</td><td align="left">6.7</td><td align="left">&#x0003c;0.0001</td></tr><tr><td align="left"><bold>No change</bold></td><td align="left">25.4</td><td align="left">20.8</td><td align="left">&#x0003c;0.0001</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p>n.s., not significant</p><p>* Several reasons may apply in an individual patient.</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec></back></article>